<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Teddy Riner announces candidacy for French presidential elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:412a51e0f032bb9cddb9a410698237839a98364b6ac41aabe3d58b1df0b48965</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261110-teddy-riner-announces-candidacy-for-french-presidential-elections--c5fe6760efe2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261110-teddy-riner-announces-candidacy-for-french-presidential-elections" /><summary type="html">Teddy Riner has announced his candidacy for the 2027 French presidential elections, against a backdrop of political tension across France.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Ukraine, Russia and US to resume peace talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:048da60a4c0d6beefaf74c58374177cbae859db300a8e37d83b204344e716bec</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi--54a00d669ba5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are meeting in Abu Dhabi for their first trilateral talks in more than nine months, as Washington pushes for an end to the war and Kyiv faces pressure to make territorial concessions. European representatives will also attend, amid fears that US President Donald Trump could press Ukraine to accept a deal on Moscow's terms. Follow our live blog for the latest events.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macrons file new defamation lawsuit against US podcaster over transgender rumours</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b35636881ea89c1efe7e7a88c203bac5f9d0821bc904aad5bc092bb4d3627a47</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T04:33:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261110-macrons-file-new-defamation-lawsuit-against-us-podcaster-over-transgender-rumours--fd3395503ce3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261110-macrons-file-new-defamation-lawsuit-against-us-podcaster-over-transgender-rumours" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and his wife Brigitte filed a second lawsuit against US right-wing podcaster Candace Owens over false claims on her gender, accusing her of continuing to spread the allegations and profiting from them despite earlier legal action.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>California voters reject proposed one-time tax on billionaires' wealth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b5a9627a277b5c841071a44bc03bec4625d1e0a60840dcb5cee2e56aac09e38</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:19:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-california-voters-reject-proposed-one-time-tax-on-billionaires-wealth--23d9a4920bc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-california-voters-reject-proposed-one-time-tax-on-billionaires-wealth" /><summary type="html">California voters have rejected a proposed 5% tax on the net worth of billionaires, handing a victory to tech leaders who poured hundreds of millions of dollars into defeating the measure. The defeat of Proposition 40 also marks a setback for progressives seeking to tax the wealth of the ultra-rich.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Amnesty urges El Salvador to disclose terms of Haiti troop deployment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbe7e2a209a89c2f4d780cf4263cf703e1a4c8358b2c79f7f7a4fabeb5aade08</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T02:24:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-amnesty-urges-el-salvador-to-disclose-terms-of-haiti-troop-deployment--f3928145d38d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-amnesty-urges-el-salvador-to-disclose-terms-of-haiti-troop-deployment" /><summary type="html">Amnesty International has called on El Salvador and Haiti to make public the agreement governing the deployment of around 2,000 Salvadoran troops to the gang-plagued Caribbean nation, warning of risks to human rights and accountability.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia shares slide as board probes CEO over affair with alleged Chinese spy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f469bb781b5c53e9b413a0bd3c20eed94c1ba4d64a05c7382a028a9071f7308</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T00:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-nvidia-shares-slide-as-board-probes-ceo-over-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy--5933ab068fa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-nvidia-shares-slide-as-board-probes-ceo-over-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang is facing scrutiny after reports he was targeted in a suspected Chinese intelligence operation involving a businesswoman with whom he was having an affair. The controversy has rattled investors, sending Nvidia shares tumbling.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Defense Secretary Hegseth faces expected impeachment vote this week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a2ebd766454a71efcb116164fd13d239ee0f10b35bc4467bb4dbd361d338158</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-hegseth-faces-expected-impeachment-vote-this-week--f8706db36377.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-hegseth-faces-expected-impeachment-vote-this-week" /><summary type="html">A Republican lawmaker moved Monday to impeach US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth over the war in Iran, setting up a potentially explosive vote in Congress days after President Donald Trump's party suffered a crushing midterm defeat. Kentucky congressman Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment accusing Hegseth of illegally waging war without congressional authorization and abusing his powers as Pentagon chief. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>France blames Iran for cyberattack on supermarket fridges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f9569ed29d456d8e418db5c44458baf3b80cd1038b17ec734d1271d2342ff67</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-france-blames-iran-for-cyberattack-on-supermarket-fridges--a5317c27a190.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-france-blames-iran-for-cyberattack-on-supermarket-fridges" /><summary type="html">French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia: honeypot may have been aimed at 'lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0120a1f4e03afbe6e938208b66355be2bb868f8c7b16fcb967fb1129dc048791</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:17:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261109-nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government--caf6f248bb43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261109-nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government" /><summary type="html">Nvidia ⁠and ​Chief ​Executive Jensen Huang were ​sued ‌on ⁠Monday ‌in ⁠a proposed class ​action accusing ‌them of ‌defrauding ​shareholders by concealing Huang's ties ​with ​a ​suspected ​Chinese spy. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Steve Tsang, Director of the SOAS China Institute, says that the affair "can also be about effectively lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government, because he is a very powerful figure, particularly during the Trump administration, and he, for whatever reason, has been taking a position that is beneficial to Chinese development and advancement of its AI capacity".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia: honeypot may have been aimed at 'lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78b9494aa34f486f95b75e267ca8b13c39d704101b794595a5b5fcf0cc68044a</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government--9a338a706ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government" /><summary type="html">Nvidia ⁠and ​Chief ​Executive Jensen Huang were ​sued ‌on ⁠Monday ‌in ⁠a proposed class ​action accusing ‌them of ‌defrauding ​shareholders by concealing Huang's ties ​with ​a ​suspected ​Chinese spy. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Steve Tsang, Director of the SOAS China Institute, says that the affair "can also be about effectively lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government, because he is a very powerful figure, particularly during the Trump administration, and he, for whatever reason, has been taking a position that is beneficial to Chinese development and advancement of its AI capacity".</summary></entry><entry><title>UK writer M. John Harrison wins Booker Prize for AI-tinged apocalyptic novel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f6dce9a0546e9b6ec66c76c63d17c48c7da9c297ea4ecc60aed561909ad773e</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel--baced25ef4ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel" /><summary type="html">UK author M. John Harrison won the Booker Prize on Monday for his enigmatic novel "The End of Everything", which echoes concerns about artificial intelligence in a darkly satirical depiction of post-apocalyptic Britain.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa’s ANC suffers a historic setback in local elections as coalition talks begin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f0a57b8ac64ab5c11cdf7a1da91ac4d4be3092297e0bd7122b554505a432c69</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:54:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin--3da15ef6ee92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin" /><summary type="html">South Africa’s ruling ANC suffers its worst-ever local election results, securing just 30% of the vote, as coalition talks loom. Meanwhile, former Ugandan military intelligence officer Herbert Matanda Mabonga accuses the army of secretly detaining and torturing opponents, following the release of videos that sparked national outrage. Finally, in Senegal, more than 200,000 free tickets are giving young people the chance to experience the games live on home soil, in a bid to inspire a new generation of athletes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>What to expect as Russia, Ukraine and the US hold trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d67f9340d6001346c078364186970a69ab183fc8ec97738b88269e2448ae8cc8</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:46:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi--07b759c50f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are set to meet in the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Tuesday for a new round of talks aimed at ending nearly five years of full-scale war triggered by Moscow's invasion of its neighbour. Security guarantees for the warring sides are set to top the agenda, with US officials insisting that a broader security architecture for Europe must be part of any peace deal.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French Judo superstar Teddy Riner says will run for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5abe1fbeee25974a7c85cfa07745f6e03c0efbea119d9c2deb224b7f07cbcbf</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:14:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-judo-superstar-teddy-riner-says-will-run-for-president--7f172ae75897.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-judo-superstar-teddy-riner-says-will-run-for-president" /><summary type="html">France's multiple Olympic judo champion Teddy Riner announced on Monday he would run in next year's presidential election, after expressing concern about the "rise of the far right". "My name is Teddy Riner and today, I am telling you face to face: I am a candidate in the 2027 presidential election," the 37-year-old said in a surprise announcement on social media. Riner, one of the greatest judokas in history, said in the two-minute-37-second video that he feared France could soon become deeply divided, appearing to cast himself as a candidate for voters unwilling to choose between two political extremes -- the far right and the hard left. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Yves Sintomer, Professor of Political Science at Université Paris VIII.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says he was ‘kidding’ about Dana White press secretary job, amid online mix-up claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e20eec7cb8f757ec0303707ca97f49cd71005ffd0e4faa2edbd5692c72ed588</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:51:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261109-trump-says-he-was-kidding-about-dana-white-press-secretary-job-amid-online-mix-up-claims--6373b90e4085.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261109-trump-says-he-was-kidding-about-dana-white-press-secretary-job-amid-online-mix-up-claims" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump says he was "only kidding" when he announced he had offered his friend and UFC boss Dana White the job of White House press secretary. The president shared an AI-generated video of White behind the briefing room podium and UFC fighters attacking journalists. But the announcement also sparked online speculation that Trump may have confused the UFC executive with a former Pentagon spokesperson, also called Dana White. There's no evidence of a mix-up, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia's Huang scandal rattles AI industry built around him</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:545689180e7236eb5e4b4c3042259a555b5484ad6a208b01ea20b5ae57b3338f</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:09:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nvidia-s-huang-scandal-rattles-ai-industry-built-around-him--b18348a1ba1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nvidia-s-huang-scandal-rattles-ai-industry-built-around-him" /><summary type="html">Nvidia chief Jensen Huang sits at the center of the artificial intelligence boom, and the spy scandal that erupted over the weekend threatens to shake the company at a time when confidence in the AI investment frenzy is already fragile. Taiwan-born Huang is regarded as the godfather of the AI economy, the executive every player in the industry must turn to because the technology depends on the graphics processing units (GPUs) that his company designs. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris prosecutor opens probe into IRGC cyber unit Shahid Kaveh over fridge cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8360602b2101228441078193427c4cfd68f3868366396e8c1bad6f64b29c021d</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:06:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks--f78cb38b635a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">The Paris prosecutor said she had opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a shadowy cyber unit of the IRGC, the Islamic republic's ideological army, over the 'unprecedented' cyberattacks targeting French supermarkets' fridges in October. Little is known about the Shahid Kaveh unit, although analysts have long observed that the IRGC, which has a vast network of operations, had actively branched out into cyber warfare in recent years. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:245dd24684e12e1ac39dba7f068b74d402e778de3d7b746796e687b0f24a65df</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--03265434b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape, as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him. Brand, 51, showed no emotion as judge Joel Bennathan said he had acted with "staggering arrogance" and shown "contempt" for his victims, who had suffered significant and lasting harm. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Eisenkot succeed in 'minefield of Israeli politics' where 'so many other generals' have failed?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c29bd70df9549b272de3742f975fd04c85f3199cf6ce89e7eedb4bc5ed80c381</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-fa--ea02cbc16553.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-failed" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Dahlia Scheindlin, Israeli author, political analyst, strategic consultant and pollster, to examine a question that reaches far beyond the immediate struggle for power: Can Israel move beyond Netanyahu amid coalition deadlock, growing disillusionment in Washington and the persistent limits of political inclusion? As Gadi Eisenkot embarks on a 45-day race to form a government, following Israeli President Isaac Herzog's decision to entrust him with the task of assembling an elusive parliamentary majority, Scheindlin offers a timely reminder: “It's always too early to eulogize Netanyahu politically.” seemingly insurmountable political crises.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Republican congressman launches impeachment bid against Pentagon chief Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:078e6a8b0e5a5a472ef1dc08197cf28dc3855ea563c91f771faf324ba484fda6</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:32:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-republican-congressman-launches-impeachment-bid-against-pentagon-chief-hegseth--505cf51d6d47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-republican-congressman-launches-impeachment-bid-against-pentagon-chief-hegseth" /><summary type="html">Kentucky congressman Thomas Massie moved on Monday to force a vote in the House of Representatives to impeach Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, putting pressure on his fellow Republicans to decide whether to remove one of the Trump administration’s most prominent figures following the party's crushing defeat in midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'We think' the Iranians and Americans want to negotiate, Egyptian FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d07e7f168ba7bffae8753280575047f8369ed8f4a138e58141b7379d4e4b46d9</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:31:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says--3e2f1e24b9a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian Foreign Minister Badr Abdelatty said he believed Iran and the United States wanted to negotiate, but called for a "concrete deal" to prevent another escalation. He also said Cairo was still "counting" on US President Donald Trump to "move forward" with the stalled Gaza peace plan and was "confident" US military aid to Egypt would continue.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>France opens probe into Iranian cyber unit over fridge attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e0c6661c5baf71a1acd3f5344a22033a9021fb216f1a4379060346599eab1b2</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:24:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-opens-probe-into-iranian-cyber-unit-over-fridge-attacks--af6707e4e593.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-opens-probe-into-iranian-cyber-unit-over-fridge-attacks" /><summary type="html">France on Monday said Iran's Revolutionary Guards were behind "unprecedented" cyberattacks on supermarket fridges in the country last month, vowing sanctions on a European level against Tehran. Swathes of French supermarkets were hit in the October 11 and 12 cyberattacks, which raised the temperatures in their refrigerators, in some cases forcing them to throw away entire inventories of perishable food.</summary></entry><entry><title>Broken system? French protesters rage against austerity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c6561986b3bafd98decace73b53e17ffda4e594b4ab9dfa736b49de2a42e2df</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:33:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:19:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261109-broken-system-french-protesters-rage-against-austerity--5b3db2568aed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261109-broken-system-french-protesters-rage-against-austerity" /><summary type="html">How can the nation of haute couture and high speed rail have an affordability issue? On paper, France boasts the planet’s seventh largest economy. Its top diplomat started the week hosting a Group of Seven Industrialized Nations foreign ministers meeting inside the regal setting of its landmark Left Bank ministry.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a57f3b727e3f7514a63336fd3fcccbc86b7fff06edfb4d2be0d25d4ec00402f</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T17:26:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians--d44b8a8693f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."</summary></entry></feed>
